<title>SINGAPORE: Compact Metal 1996 profit plunges 62.4pct.</title>
<headline>Compact Metal 1996 profit plunges 62.4pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31 1996</p>
<p>(in million of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   1.73   vs    4.61</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)     0.90   vs    2.30</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)	     5.00   vs    5.00</p>
<p>    Turnover		    92.78   vs   82.41</p>
<p>    Other income incl int    1.23   vs    1.26</p>
<p>    Interest expense	   3.74   vs    2.41</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		3.19   vs    6.39</p>
<p>    Tax			    1.33   vs    1.73</p>
<p>    Minorities	  (loss) 0.12   vs    0.03 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries   (loss) 0.48   vs    nil</p>
<p>Note- Compact Metal Industries Ltd said the fall in profit for 1996 was due to higher interest expense and higher provision for doubtful debts. It expects competion to remain keen in the current year. - Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
